.\n$$\n\nThere are $10$ contestants, so $n=10.$ We want to select $3$ of those contestants for the medal positions, so we have $r=3.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different potential groups of medalists is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{10}{C}_{3} & =\\frac{10!}{(10-3)!\\,3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{7!3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8\\cdot \\cancel{7!}}{\\cancel{7!}3!} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\cdot 9\\cdot 8}{3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{720}{6} \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281242 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281243 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281244 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281245 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281246 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1041 "selection" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281245 13194139534187 true] [17592186281241 1110 #uuid "4ca03efc-e5aa-58c1-95ea-45ea8559657e" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281242 1034 "604\\,800" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534187 true] [17592186281242 1111 #uuid "66f776ad-dc76-571f-9fde-5bfc211b06e7" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281243 1034 "5\\,040" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534187 true] [17592186281243 1111 #uuid "d6b01038-7557-5fcb-96c4-39b1069df4fe" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281244 1034 "920" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534187 true] [17592186281244 1111 #uuid "2179505d-ca3f-5415-b40f-e3854a8c18e2" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281245 1034 "120" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534187 true] [17592186281245 1111 #uuid "50c1a4c1-45c6-5538-96dd-9020d1e67ee3" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281246 1034 "720" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534187 true] [17592186281246 1111 #uuid "be9649d7-6604-5bd0-9d26-6463bf74792e" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281247 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281248 13194139534187 true] [17592186281247 1089 "q-84964" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281247 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534187 true] [17592186281247 1100 "Given any two points in a plane, there is a unique line that passes through both points. Given six points in a plane, what is the maximum number of unique  lines that can be made using these points?" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281247 1113 #uuid "1131b9e8-079c-59fe-bb5c-f5a2e256cfe4" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281247 1145 "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $6$ points, so $n=6.$ We want to select $2$ of those points for each of the lines, so we have $r=2.$\n\nTherefore, the maximum number of unique lines is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{6}{C}_{2} & =\\frac{6!}{(6-2)!\\,2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6!}{4!2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{\\cancel{4!}2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{2} \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281249 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281250 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281251 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281252 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281253 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1041 "selection" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281250 13194139534187 true] [17592186281248 1110 #uuid "11061a03-f613-5b52-b69f-6d33ab01b754" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281249 1034 "12" 13194139534187 true] [17592186281249 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534187 true] [17592186281249 1111 #uuid "412d424a-eee3-5e6b-9875-27c053c